+# Luna hockey reference v2
+
+Luna interprets supplied hockey reports into source-backed proposals for human review. It has no publishing, alias-learning, replacement or database authority. This package extends the existing manual, default-off review flow; it does not activate hosted dispatch.
+
+## Runtime package
+
+- [`tweetLunaReference.ts`](./tweetLunaReference.ts) is the executable starter instruction and reference builder. Stable rule IDs cover purpose, untrusted text, response shape, dated identity, exact evidence, goalie wording, game/session scope, broader hockey context, corrections and uncertainty.
+- `luna-hockey-reference-v2` / `luna-hockey-rules-v2` pin the rules, correction categories and selected reference mode through a content hash. The default `development` mode also pins example guidance and the retained library. `referenceMode: "rules-and-synthetic-only"` omits the entire S01–S10 library, source pins, examples and labels; its package hash is distinct and `libraryVersion` is null. Invalid modes hold before dispatch. Review results record `referencePackage` and `responsesRequestHash` (the caller wire before fixed transport controls); the queue key includes the package identity. A package change creates a different review key and transport request, without resetting any ledger or granting a new paid attempt.
+- [`tweetLunaReview.ts`](./tweetLunaReview.ts) builds the Responses input after the existing retained-source and dated-evidence checks. `buildLunaReviewRequest` is pure and inspectable offline. The unchanged Decisions reference receives only its original bound deterministic claims, never Luna's proposals or development labels.
+- [`tweetLunaAdjudicatedLibrary.json`](./fixtures/tweetLunaAdjudicatedLibrary.json) remains the sole S01–S10 source library. The builder selects named claim pointers and preserves original records, hashes, author/time bases, source-unit labels, conventions, analyst inferences, prerequisites and S10's relation. It excludes the whole group when the current original post ID or exact text matches any record in that group. This is a same-case leakage guard, not proof of general evaluation independence.
+
+Trusted instructions contain only application rules. Reports, candidate strings, source provenance and development examples travel as JSON input data, never interpolated into trusted instructions. Runtime source content must not instruct Luna to change the contract or perform actions. The nested identity contract's instructions apply only to `identity`; its identity-only response instruction is no longer concatenated into the trusted outer instructions. The original identity request/hash and validator remain unchanged.
+
+Reference context consumes part of the existing 64 KiB transport limit. Oversized requests remain held before admission/key access; no silent truncation, extra request, retry or larger budget is introduced.
+
+## Supplied identity and source interfaces
+
+The input envelope contains:
+
+| Field | Authority and use |
+| --- | --- |
+| `identityRequest` | Existing [`FixtureIdentityRequest`](./tweetIdentityProposal.ts): exact source/occurrences, per-occurrence canonical candidates, directory version/hash/as-of/completeness and relevance hints. No lookup from model memory. |
+| `identityRequestHash` | Copy into the existing response `identity.requestHash`. It hashes `identityRequest`, not the surrounding reference envelope. |
+| `sourcePolicy` | Typed `LunaSuppliedSourcePolicy`: retained source/revision and packet hash, original reporter/URL/publication clock, ingestion clock and existing attribution provenance. Also carries identity evaluation mode and as-of. Values are supplied evidence, not model-authenticated truth. |
+| `sourcePolicy.identityEvaluation` | Existing [`IdentityEvidenceEvaluation`](./playerIdentitySnapshotEvidence.ts), either causal at publication or explicitly retrospective with review time. Saved evidence still enforces knowledge cutoff and independently evidenced effective intervals before candidates are built. |
+| `referencePackage` / `identityInstructionsScope` | Version/hash/mode, and explicit `identity_field_only` scope for the nested identity instructions. |
+| `developmentLibrary` / `developmentExamples` | Present only in development mode: previously exposed mixed-provenance material, with explicit limits. No canonical identity or game facts can be imported from these examples into the current report. |
+
+Game/source/time acceptance and conflict/retraction checks remain mandatory downstream holds. This interface cannot supply a verified game ID or grant source trust. Missing reporter/time or invalid retained lineage still holds before dispatch. Current membership is not historical membership, receipt time is not publication time, and a timezone-free relative phrase does not identify a game.
+
+## Unchanged response and interpretation limits
+
+The strict response remains `{identity, goalieStatuses}`. Identity retains exactly the existing fields/status enums; each goalie proposal is only `{occurrenceId, canonicalId, status, evidence}`. `goalieStatuses` is required and can be empty. No additional explanation, injury, lineup, PP, timing, confidence number or correction fields are accepted. Broader claims need a separately coordinated schema, validator and test change.
+
+First-off supports projected; practice and warmup attendance alone do not establish starts. Explicit starter wording during warmups may pass the existing deterministic wording gate, but remains unverified and game-unbound. S01's reviewed leading-out convention does not override that gate. Tentative proposals require an adjacent explicit likely/probable or expected/projected starting predicate in both the exact evidence and subject sentence. Name-only, attendance, backup, negated-start and unrelated probability wording cannot supply likely/projected. First-off evidence must actually contain first-off wording. Full-source wording must agree with a definite proposal so a clipped conditional cannot supply certainty.
+
+[`tweetLunaGoalieWording.ts`](./tweetLunaGoalieWording.ts) adds conservative lexical gates around the unchanged parser. It rejects conditional/disavowed/historical/in-game subject sentences and keeps negation outside a clipped quote in view. Repeated matched canonical identities or a correction/update/retraction marker anywhere in a report require omitted/unknown goalie proposals. This deliberately also holds harmless updates and consistent repeated mentions: the strict schema has no correction relation or phase field. It does not adjudicate which version is true.
+
+All reports require reading their complete context. Preserve negation, uncertainty, original attribution, conflicting/revised sources and the distinction between game entry, in-game changes and next-game projections. If the current schema cannot safely express that context, omit a goalie proposal or retain unknown. PP versus even-strength role, practice versus selection, injury versus availability, and reassessment versus return date are teaching context only in the unchanged response schema v1.
+
+These instructions and finite deterministic guards do not prove model adherence or understand every hockey sentence. Punctuation-based context, unlisted paraphrases, pronoun-only contradictions, omitted occurrence extraction, cross-sentence/cross-report negation and complex temporal relationships can still require human interpretation. General prompt injection resistance is not established by prescribed-response tests. `verified:false`, null game/team/override, and the existing acceptance holds remain the operational boundary. Identity confidence is an uncalibrated enum; downstream likely/projected floors are not model confidence or publication authority.
+
+## Reviewed development material and evaluation gap
+
+S01–S10 are ten human-reviewed source groups with twelve retained records. Detailed claim labels are assistant-derived under recorded owner distinctions; this is neither independent world truth nor proof the owner individually graded every field. The package preserves that provenance, including unknown canonical bindings and the original source clock/receipt caveats. No new source fetch, redistribution permission or rights clearance is inferred from the files' presence. Existing local use is continued; external reuse needs its own provenance/rights check.
+
+The package lessons cover warmups (S01), uncertainty and practice (S02), explicit starter wording (S03), PP roles (S04), subject-bound injury timelines (S05), paired replacement (S06), unresolved availability (S07), lineup/goalie listing (S08), first-off (S09) and correction/drill context (S10).
+
+No genuinely separated, independently reviewed evaluation set with established provenance/rights was available in the supplied material. [`tweetLunaSyntheticCases.ts`](./fixtures/tweetLunaSyntheticCases.ts) is newly authored synthetic regression data, excluded from the runtime package. The nearest suite injects prescribed Responses outputs through the real review/transport validation path. It measures deterministic contract acceptance/rejection, exact evidence and provenance binding, abstention, clocks, correction retention, schema escape rejection and offline integration. It does **not** measure Luna's accuracy, prompt adherence or generalization. S01–S10 checks measure preservation of retained labels, not predictions.
+
+[`tweetLunaEvaluation.ts`](./fixtures/tweetLunaEvaluation.ts) freezes a separately named **synthetic development batch**, not a holdout: 16 fictional reports/identities/receipts, explicit expected identity/goalie/Decisions labels, four eligible deterministic Decisions bindings, package hash and a 20-call/concurrency-one/zero-retry budget including prior exposure. Labels are assistant-authored before predictions and pending independent review. Negative-start and first-off claims stay in Responses; the unchanged deterministic mapper does not qualify them for Decisions. No source is fetched, and no S01–S10 data is transmitted by this variant. Broader injury/lineup/PP cases remain context-only.
+
+[`rehearse-luna-evaluation.ts`](../../scripts/rehearse-luna-evaluation.ts) has only an offline `--output NEW_DIRECTORY` mode, no credential/environment loader or paid dispatch option. It writes the frozen batch before prescribed responders run, exercises the actual caller/transport/admission, saves exact transport bodies/hashes and compares results with frozen labels. Invalid/uncertain outcomes or label mismatch stop the batch; no automatic retry exists. The task retains requests, labels, results and a clearly marked synthetic ledger. Usage and confidence values are mock data; diagnostic cost estimates are not a proved token ceiling or real invoice. Real admission uses the existing full-context reservation and aggregate cap. A paid executor/ledger continuation remains a separate reviewed handoff.
+
+A future qualification set should be separately acquired under permitted use, reviewed without model outputs or development answer hints, and split by original source/quote/revision chain and event family before prompt tuning. Record reviewer/date, rights basis, source hash/time basis and all unresolved canonical/game fields. Freeze its manifest; keep it out of prompt selection and tuning. Only an authorized model evaluation can measure field accuracy, abstention precision/coverage, false certainty, cross-subject errors and conflict/correction handling on that set. Current funding/access observations and action-time gates belong in the task's preflight/handoff, not in model instructions.
+
+## Future field review
+
+The exported correction categories cover identity, evidence, attribution, time/scope, goalie status, conflict/correction, unsupported claims, abstention and injection/schema violations. A future review record should bind `reviewQueueKey`, package version/hash, Responses request hash, packet/source revision, occurrence ID and field path, before/proposed values, exact evidence, category, reviewer, reviewed-at timestamp, decision (accept/reject/correct/defer), rationale and any linked conflicting/replacement review IDs. Preserve the original proposal and disagreements. Game/source/time clearance must remain a separate trusted acceptance decision.
+
+These are a review-record specification and a correction taxonomy, not a new UI or persistence system. A swipe is field feedback only: no automatic training, alias learning, publication or production authorization. Changes to reference material require explicit review, provenance, a new version/hash, and the offline regression checks. Invalid provider responses remain held; a held artifact must never be treated as an accepted field proposal.
+
+## Local validation
+
+From `web/`, use the task's offline configuration, which disables `.env` loading and inherits a network-denial tripwire:
+
+```sh
+env -i PATH="$PATH" TMPDIR=/tmp NODE_OPTIONS='--require=/Users/tim/Code/fhfhockey.com/tasks/artifacts/luna-reference-package-2026-10-31/deny-network.cjs' ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run --config ../tasks/artifacts/luna-reference-package-2026-10-31/offline.config.mts lib/sources/tweetLunaReview.test.ts
+./node_modules/.bin/tsc --noEmit -p ../tasks/artifacts/luna-reference-package-2026-10-31/tsconfig.json
+./node_modules/.bin/eslint lib/sources/tweetLunaReference.ts lib/sources/tweetLunaGoalieWording.ts lib/sources/tweetLunaReview.ts lib/sources/tweetLunaReview.test.ts lib/sources/fixtures/tweetLunaSyntheticCases.ts lib/sources/fixtures/tweetLunaEvaluation.ts scripts/rehearse-luna-evaluation.ts
+```
+
+See the [repair handoff](../../../tasks/artifacts/luna-reference-package-2026-10-31/repair-r1/HANDOFF.md) for actual results, standalone rehearsal command, credential boundary and file pins. The original [task handoff](../../../tasks/artifacts/luna-reference-package-2026-10-31/HANDOFF.md) retains v1 evidence. The historical integration handoff is available via `git show cb8ed5217:tasks/artifacts/luna-review-integration-2026-10-23/HANDOFF.md`; its original worktree file is absent from this checkout.
